      "message": "feat(browser): migrate the supervisor keepalive session to the GLM agent platform\n\nThe supervisor's own conversation now runs on chat.z.ai like the fleet:\n\n- agent-session-monitor.mjs (new): digest-based GLM session monitor with\n  the ChatGptSessionMonitor public contract. GENERATING is entered only\n  through markGenerationStarted after a proven Enter submit; digest churn\n  / network / external progress refresh progress; a quiet settle window\n  flips IDLE terminal-ready; adaptive soft/hard stall floors unchanged.\n  Recovery is ESCALATE-only - chat.z.ai has no addressable stop or\n  continuation control, and navigation-class recovery stays forbidden.\n- supervisor-lifecycle-runtime-core: conversation/root regexes, auth-tab\n  reuse, NEW_TAB surfaces and the wake submit move to the platform; the\n  ambiguous-wake and rollover continuations re-submit through the Enter\n  lane when the composer still holds the exact message (sha256 proof the\n  prior submit never happened) instead of clicking a named Send control;\n  the keepalive conversation validator accepts chat.z.ai/c/<id>.\n- supervisor-keepalive: conversation URL contract is the GLM platform\n  shape; snapshot schema default is the agent session monitor.\n- tests: supervisor/keepalive/bootstrap/continuity suites migrated to\n  chat.z.ai fixtures and the GLM submit contract; the restart suite now\n  proves the ambiguous predecessor is fenced into history while exactly\n  one fresh current-process wake is emitted with a proven submit.\n\nFull suite 2373 pass / 0 fail / 2 pre-existing skips; security static\ngate clean; npm run check clean.",
